# =============================================================================
# CineSpine Environment Configuration
# =============================================================================

# Google Gemini & Imagen 3 API Key (Get free from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey)
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Optional: ClickHouse OLAP event spine. Setting CLICKHOUSE_HOST is what turns
# it on; without it the in-memory spine serves every read and nothing is lost.
# An unreachable host degrades the same way rather than failing startup.
#
# Local, from docker-compose.yml:
# CLICKHOUSE_HOST=localhost
# CLICKHOUSE_PORT=8123
# CLICKHOUSE_USER=default
# CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD=
# CLICKHOUSE_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=5
#
# Or a hosted instance. CLICKHOUSE_SECURE moves the default port to 8443 with
# it, so these three lines are the whole change -- leave CLICKHOUSE_PORT unset
# unless the provider says otherwise. TLS is stated rather than guessed from
# the hostname: guessing means a list of what hosted endpoints look like, and
# that list is wrong the day a provider adds a domain.
# CLICKHOUSE_HOST=abc123.europe-west4.gcp.clickhouse.cloud
# CLICKHOUSE_SECURE=1
# CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD=your_password
#
# Only for a self-hosted instance with its own certificate authority. A hosted
# endpoint has a public certificate and needs nothing; turning this off makes
# TLS prove nothing about who answered.
# CLICKHOUSE_VERIFY=0

# Optional: official ClickHouse MCP server for the Wrap Rescue Agent.
#
# Start the official mcp-clickhouse server against the same ClickHouse cluster,
# then point CineSpine at its HTTP MCP endpoint. When unset, the agent returns
# an unavailable trace and does not rank or mutate requirements.
#
# CLICKHOUSE_MCP_URL=https://mcp.clickhouse.cloud/mcp
# http://localhost:4200/mcp
# CLICKHOUSE_MCP_AUTH_TOKEN=
# CLICKHOUSE_MCP_TIMEOUT=10

# Optional: Grafana Cloud Observability (OTLP and Faro)
# To get these credentials:
# 1. Go to your Grafana Cloud Portal -> Details -> OpenTelemetry
# 2. Generate a token with metrics/logs/traces write access.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=https://otlp-gateway-prod-us-east-0.grafana.net/otlp
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS="Authorization=Basic <base64-encoded-instance-id:token>"
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=http/protobuf
# VITE_GRAFANA_FARO_URL=https://faro-collector-prod-us-east-0.grafana.net/collect/...

# Optional: turn off the AI features that make billed calls during upload.
# CINESPINE_DISABLE_AI_CHARACTER_INFERENCE=1
# CINESPINE_DISABLE_LINING_EXTRACTION=1
# CINESPINE_DISABLE_CAMERA_REPORT_VISION=1

# Optional: opt into a Pro model for complex tasks. Off by default because a
# free-tier key is quota'd at zero on Pro, not merely rate-limited.
# CINESPINE_GEMINI_PRO_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro

# Optional: run Gemini through Vertex AI / Gemini Enterprise credentials.
# Vertex publishes no `-latest` alias for any Gemini model, so every id here is
# a real Model Garden publisher model. `gcloud ai model-garden models list
# --model-filter=gemini` is the catalogue to check against.
# GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=TRUE
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=cinespine
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=europe-west4
# CINESPINE_WRAP_RESCUE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Optional: product analytics, sent to PostHog.
#
# Both are required. The host is not optional even though the library has a
# default, because the default is a third party: where this goes should be
# something somebody wrote down rather than something that happened.
#
# Autocapture and session replay are switched off in code, not by config:
# this interface renders unreleased footage and documents carrying crew
# contact details, and a session recording is a recording of those. Properties
# are filtered centrally too -- what leaves is which production, which day,
# which department, which surface, and a role token for who. Not what any of
# it says.
#
# Self-hosted, started by docker-compose.posthog.yml (8010, because PostHog's
# own default is 8000 and that is this app's backend):
# POSTHOG_API_KEY=phc_your_project_key
# POSTHOG_HOST=http://localhost:8010
#
# Or PostHog's cloud, if that is the deployment you have chosen:
# POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
#
# The frontend reads its own pair at build time (Vite only exposes VITE_*), so
# changing these needs a rebuild:
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_your_project_key
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=http://localhost:8010

# Optional: serve the source documents themselves over the API.
#
# Off by default. A parsed fact is a slate, a roll, a timecode. A source
# document is the page those were read off, and it carries what the parsers
# were written to leave behind: crew phone numbers and emails in the footer,
# cast names, locations, unreleased plot. Serving the file serves all of it.
#
# The embedded demo fixtures are synthetic and are served regardless, so the
# default costs the demo nothing and refuses everywhere the paperwork is real.
#
# CINESPINE_SERVE_SOURCE_DOCUMENTS=1
